From: Eduardo Fockink <54868856+EduardoFockink@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: add AQ_MGPU_GPU_COPY, a zero-CPU-copy path via Vulkan for secondary-GPU outputs

The primary GPU's Vulkan driver allocates LINEAR buffers in system RAM, exports them as dma-bufs and the
secondary scans them out. Each frame the primary's copy engine copies the damaged rectangles of its native
frame into one, waiting on the render fence on the GPU; KMS waits on the copy's sync_file. Falls back to
AQ_MGPU_CPU_COPY when anything fails.

1.3 -> 1.4: the linear buffers now set IBuffer::size (it stayed 0x0, and the atomic commit sizes the plane
from it: black screen), and a size mismatch falls back instead of committing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
